        <mxCell id="e7back" value="Next Sprint" style="endArrow=block;endFill=1;html=1;strokeWidth=2;strokeColor=#DC2626;fontStyle=1;fontSize=10;fontColor=#DC2626;exitX=0.5;exitY=0;entryX=0.5;entryY=1;curved=1;" edge="1" parent="1" source="p7" target="p2"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="why" value="WHY AGILE / SCRUM WAS CHOSEN" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fillColor=#F0FDF4;strokeColor=#16A34A;strokeWidth=2;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=14;spacingTop=10;fontSize=12;fontStyle=1;fontColor=#14532D;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="120" y="600" width="800" height="200" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="why_d" value="1. Evolving Requirements: LGU disaster protocols needed iterative refinement through stakeholder consultations.
2. Early Risk Detection: 2-week sprints exposed issues like QR anti-duplicate race conditions early.
3. Continuous Deployment: GitHub CI/CD pipeline pushed to Vercel (web) and Render (backend) after each sprint.
4. Stakeholder Alignment: Sprint reviews with LGU officials ensured every feature matched real disaster workflows.
5. Working Software Priority: Agile delivers a testable product each sprint — critical for capstone demonstration." style="text;html=0;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=left;verticalAlign=top;whiteSpace=wrap;fontSize=10;fontColor=#374151;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="134" y="630" width="775" height="165" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="roles" value="SCRUM TEAM ROLES" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fillColor=#EFF6FF;strokeColor=#2563EB;strokeWidth=2;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=14;spacingTop=10;fontSize=12;fontStyle=1;fontColor=#1E3A8A;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="980" y="600" width="610" height="200" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="roles_d" value="Product Owner:
Manages product backlog and represents LGU/DSWD stakeholder interests.

Scrum Master:
Facilitates ceremonies, removes blockers, enforces Agile principles.

Development Team:
Full-stack engineers — design, code, test, and deploy each sprint increment." style="text;html=0;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=left;verticalAlign=top;whiteSpace=wrap;fontSize=10;fontColor=#374151;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="994" y="630" width="595" height="165" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
